From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:13:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(allwinner): A733: apply Cortex-A76 errata

The A733's two big cores read MIDR_EL1 0x414fd0b1, Cortex-A76 r4p1. The
platform enabled no A76 erratum. Four items of the Arm Cortex-A76
Software Developer Errata Notice (SDEN-885749) are present in r4p1 and
open, and TF-A carries a workaround for each behind a flag that
defaults to 0:

- 1946160 (Cat B), "Atomic instructions with acquire semantics might
  not be ordered with respect to older stores with release semantics":
  the reset handler programs three instruction-patch slots
  (S3_6_C15_C8_0..3) so the core inserts a DMB ST before an acquire
  atomic without release semantics. It runs on the cold boot and on
  every wake from power-down.
- 2743102 (Cat B), "The core might deadlock during powerdown sequence":
  a DSB before the ISB that follows CPUPWRCTLR_EL1.CORE_PWRDN_EN in
  cortex_a76_core_pwr_dwn. With native CPU_SUSPEND that sequence runs on
  every A76 deep-idle entry, not only on CPU_OFF.
- 2356586 (Cat B), "Continuous failing STREX because of another PE
  executing prefetch for store behind consistently mispredicted branch":
  the reset handler sets CPUACTLR2_EL1[0], so PLDW / PRFM PST behave like
  PLD / PRFM PLD. Arm notes a small slowdown for some workloads that
  share data.
- 4193800 = CVE-2025-10263 (Cat B), "Completion of affected memory
  accesses might not be guaranteed by completion of a TLBI": software
  that issues a broadcast TLBI must follow it with one more TLBI and DSB,
  and if any core in the system is affected, all of them must, hence a
  platform flag. In this BL31 it changes nothing that runs: the xlat
  TLBI path is compiled only with PLAT_XLAT_TABLES_DYNAMIC, which the
  A733 does not set, so the linked BL31 has no broadcast TLBI. It is on
  so a future one is covered and the errata report is true. Linux does
  its own side (ARM64_ERRATUM_4118414).

cortex_a76.S checks the revision at run time, so the A55 cores never run
any of these. The A55 erratum 1530923 stays on; the A55 cores are r2p0,
and no other A55 erratum applies to r2p0.

The vendor BL31 is a blob (v2.5), built before most of these
workarounds existed; whether it applies any cannot be checked.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk b/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk
index f57854e34..a18b4cd64 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk
+++ b/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk
@@ -61,6 +61,33 @@ BL31_SOURCES		+=	${AW_PLAT}/${PLAT}/sunxi_cpu_back_pll.c
 # Cortex-A55 r2p0
 ERRATA_A55_1530923	:=	1
 
+# Cortex-A76 errata open on the A733's big cores, r4p1 (MIDR_EL1 0x414fd0b1),
+# from the Arm Cortex-A76 Software Developer Errata Notice SDEN-885749.
+# cortex_a76.S checks the revision, so each is applied only where it matches.
+#   1946160 (Cat B): an atomic with acquire semantics might not be ordered
+#     against an older store with release semantics. The reset handler
+#     programs three instruction-patch slots (S3_6_C15_C8_0-3) that insert a
+#     DMB ST before acquire atomics without release semantics.
+#   2743102 (Cat B): the core might deadlock in the hardware cache flush of
+#     its power-down sequence. A DSB before the ISB that follows
+#     CPUPWRCTLR_EL1.CORE_PWRDN_EN in cortex_a76_core_pwr_dwn, which runs on
+#     every A76 CPU_SUSPEND power-down and on CPU_OFF.
+#   2356586 (Cat B): continuous failing STREX because another PE executes a
+#     prefetch for store behind a consistently mispredicted branch. The
+#     reset handler sets CPUACTLR2_EL1[0], so PLDW / PRFM PST behave like
+#     PLD / PRFM PLD.
+#   4193800 = CVE-2025-10263 (Cat B): completion of affected memory accesses
+#     might not be guaranteed by completion of a TLBI; software that issues a
+#     broadcast TLBI must repeat TLBI + DSB. Platform wide, because one
+#     affected core in the system is enough. In this BL31 there is no
+#     broadcast TLBI (the xlat TLBI path needs PLAT_XLAT_TABLES_DYNAMIC), so
+#     it is on to keep any future one covered.
+# The A55 cores are r2p0; no other A55 erratum applies to r2p0.
+ERRATA_A76_1946160		:=	1
+ERRATA_A76_2743102		:=	1
+ERRATA_A76_2356586		:=	1
+WORKAROUND_CVE_2025_10263	:=	1
+
 USE_COHERENT_MEM		:=	0
 WARMBOOT_ENABLE_DCACHE_EARLY	:=	1
 HW_ASSISTED_COHERENCY		:=	1
